---
import Profile from '../layouts/Profile.astro';
import WorkstationMedia from '../components/WorkstationMedia.astro';
import SelectedProducts from '../components/SelectedProducts.astro';
import NoteList from '../components/NoteList.astro';
import { getPublishedNotes } from '../lib/notes';
import '../styles/workstation.css';
import '../styles/notes.css';
const notes = (await getPublishedNotes()).slice(0, 3);
---
<Profile page="home" footerMessage={{title: 'Get in touch', body: 'I’m looking for my next role building AI tools and agent workflows, drawing on accounting and enterprise implementation. Based in Des Moines.'}}>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <h1>I build AI tools and agent workflows grounded in accounting and enterprise implementation.</h1>
      <p class="lede">10+ years in reporting and customer delivery, including implementation leadership. Homebase is my main project, connecting business operations and agent work. I build with Codex and Claude, and publish this site on <a href="/notes/cloudflare-build-workflow/">Cloudflare Workers</a>. Follow the work in my <a href="/notes/">build notes</a>.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#selected-work">View selected work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="scene-wrap"><WorkstationMedia /></div>
  </section>
  <section id="selected-work" class="section selected-work wrap">
    <h2>Selected work</h2>
    <SelectedProducts />
  </section>
  <section id="building" class="section implementation wrap">
    <h2>Building with Cloudflare and AI tools</h2>
    <p>I use <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/">Cloudflare Workers</a> to publish this Astro site, with Wrangler handling deployment. The pages and build notes arrive as readable HTML, including when JavaScript is unavailable.</p>
    <p>I own product direction and implementation for Homebase, Passal, and Leasekite, working through AI coding tools. Codex and Claude help with implementation and review. Homebase uses React and TypeScript; Passal uses Next.js.</p>
    <p>GitHub keeps the source and change history. Playwright and axe check browser behavior and accessibility, and I inspect the live result after deployment.</p>
    <div class="case-links"><a href="/notes/cloudflare-build-workflow/">How I ship this site with Cloudflare</a><a href="/fit/#building">My building approach</a><a href="/ai-workflows/">AI workflows and agent stack</a><a href="/dave-bettner-resume.pdf" download>Download résumé</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="build-notes-heading">
    <h2 id="build-notes-heading">Build notes</h2>
    <NoteList notes={notes} headingLevel="h3" />
    <div class="case-links"><a href="/notes/">All build notes</a><a href="/now/">What I’m working on now</a><a href="/rss.xml">Follow via RSS</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section background-tools wrap">
    <div class="experience">
      <h2>Customer delivery background</h2>
      <p>At Citrin Cooperman, I managed a five-person implementation team. At Workiva, I led 6–12 concurrent implementations. At LSL, I led Workiva delivery for city and county finance teams.</p>
      <p>At LSL, I scoped consulting engagements, prepared estimates and statements of work, and led Workiva delivery for city and county finance teams through client sign-off. I also directed AI-assisted development of Python reporting tools reused across engagements. I built internal review workflows that compare reports with source records and route discrepancies for human review before client changes.</p>
      <div class="case-links"><a href="/experience/">Career history</a><a href="/experience/connected-reporting/">Connected-reporting implementation</a><a href="/fit/#scope">Scope and client enablement</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="technical-work">
      <h2>Technical tools</h2>
      <div class="projects">
        <article class="project">
          <div>
            <h3><a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/">Accounting Acceptance Lab</a></h3>
            <p>Testing whether accounting agents use the right evidence and recover without duplicate ledger changes. Synthetic accounting cases.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/" aria-label="About the project: Accounting Acceptance Lab">Details</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/accounting-acceptance-lab" aria-label="View repository: Accounting Acceptance Lab">View repository</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="project">
          <div>
            <h3><a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/">Regulated Reporting MCP</a></h3>
            <p>Exploring limits on AI agents changing reports, with caller-confirmed default writes. Mock-data demo.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/" aria-label="About the project: Regulated Reporting MCP">Details</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/regulated-reporting-mcp" aria-label="View repository: Regulated Reporting MCP">View repository</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <a class="section-link" href="/work/">More technical work</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap teaching" aria-labelledby="teaching-heading">
    <h2 id="teaching-heading">Technical walkthroughs</h2>
    <div class="projects">
      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/learn/verify-an-ai-update/">How do you know an AI update worked?</a></h3>
          <p>Try a valid update, a stale source, a wrong calculation, and a lost response. This interactive lesson explains how to check an automated action and recover without applying it twice.</p>
          <p class="project-limit">Fictional inventory data. Deterministic checks run in your browser.</p>
        </div>
        <div><a href="/learn/verify-an-ai-update/">Try the walkthrough</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/ai-workflows/">Inside an AI workflow</a></h3>
          <p>How I connect source records, agent tools, review, and recovery. Examples from internal reporting work sit alongside public projects with inspectable code.</p>
        </div>
        <div><a href="/ai-workflows/">Read the workflow guide</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Profile>
